-- title:
--   Diamond model automorphism moves places by the inverse diamond automorphism
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, an integer $M$ with $NeZero M$, $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$, a field $L$ of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ for $\{p\}$, a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta \in L$, and an intermediate field $K$ of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), the $L$-subfield of $L$-Laurent series generated by the coefficientwise images of the $q$-expansion function field of $X_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A$, with $A$ acting on $K$ compatibly through $L$, and let $j \in K$ be nonzero with Laurent series the coefficientwise image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157); fix also compatible algebra structures of $A$ and $L$ on $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Let $M\eta$ be a curve model over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L182), that is, an integral scheme proper and smooth of relative dimension $1$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ whose function field is identified with that field and whose closed points are in bijection with the places, and let $e\eta$ be an isomorphism from $M\eta.C$ to the pullback of [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252) along $\operatorname{Spec}\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ such that $e\eta$ followed by the second projection is the structure morphism of $M\eta$. Assume the preimage under $e\eta$ followed by the first projection of the image of the finite chart immersion [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.ιFin A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L231) is nonempty, and the pinning hypothesis that for every $a$ in the finite chart algebra [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.chartAlgFin A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L135) (the elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$) the function-field element obtained from $a$ by transport along $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}$ and $e\eta$ followed by the first projection, taking the germ at the generic point and reading it in `x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)` through the model's identification, has Laurent series the coefficientwise image under $L \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the Laurent series of $a$. Let $d$ be coprime to $Mp$ and $\theta$ an $L$-algebra automorphism of $K$ which, on Laurent series, agrees with [`ModularCurve.baseChangeAut L (ModularCurve.diamondAut (M * p) d)`](def/ModularCurve_X1Diamond.html#L24), the chosen base change to $L$ of the chosen diamond automorphism $\langle d \rangle$ of the function field of $X_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $w$ be an automorphism of the two-chart model [`ModularCurve.TwoChartModel A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L229) over $\operatorname{Spec} A$, and $\rho$ a ring automorphism of the finite chart algebra whose induced map on $K$ is $\theta$, such that $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}$ followed by $w$ equals $\operatorname{Spec}(\rho)$ followed by $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}$. Finally let $x, x'$ be $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points of $M\eta.C$ (sections of its structure morphism) such that $x'$ followed by $e\eta$ and the first projection equals $x$ followed by $e\eta$, the first projection and $w$. Then the place of `x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)` attached to $x'$ by the model's point-to-place bijection equals the image of the place attached to $x$ under the inverse of the semilinear automorphism `SemilinearAut.ofAlgAut (ModularCurve.diamondAutBar (M * p) d)`, i.e. the pair consisting of `diamondAutBar (M * p) d` on the function field and the identity on $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, acting on places.
--
--   This identifies the effect on places of the automorphism of the geometric generic fibre of the two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$ induced by the diamond operator $\langle d \rangle$: transporting a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point by the model automorphism $w$ transforms its place by the inverse of the diamond automorphism of the function field. It is used in the construction of the diamond action in the geometric setting, in the statement producing an algebra automorphism compatible with Gauss reduction and reduction of points, and in the compatibility of the Abel–Jacobi transport with the diamond generator.
